                <pb facs="0486" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.428/587</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Appointed Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geddes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 250</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to refer to Mr. Long’s
                    note of March 24th communicating a proposed amendment to Article 2 of the
                    Sockeye Salmon Treaty and to inform you that the Government of the Dominion of
                    Canada are prepared to accept this amendment.</p>
                <p>At the same time I am requested by the Canadian Government to urge that as early
                    a date as possible may now be definitely fixed for the signature of the Treaty
                    as amended.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. C. Geddes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
